  "blocks": {
    "\"Bypass mode, but only inside the sandbox.\"": "“使用绕过权限模式，但只能在沙箱里。”",
    "\"It keeps editing files when I just want a plan.\"": "“我只想先得到计划，它却一直修改文件。”",
    "\"Switch to plan mode — it'll block writes and stay in research.\"": "“切换到规划模式——它会禁止写入，并保持在研究阶段。”",
    "\"What about for the AFK run later?\"": "“之后要让它 AFK 运行呢？”",
    "A preset that shapes how the agent operates at runtime — bundles a permission mode with behavioral instructions injected into the system prompt. Examples: a default that prompts on risky calls, a plan mode that blocks edits and steers the agent toward research, an accept-edits mode that auto-approves edits, a bypass permissions mode (colloquially YOLO mode) that auto-approves everything. Can flip mid-session.": "智能体模式是一组用于塑造<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/agent\">智能体</a>运行时行为的预设，它把<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/permission-mode\">权限模式</a>与注入<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/system-prompt\">系统提示词</a>的行为指令组合在一起。例如：默认模式会在高风险调用前询问；规划模式会禁止编辑并引导智能体开展研究；接受编辑模式会自动批准文件修改；绕过权限模式（俗称 YOLO 模式）则自动批准所有操作。模式可以在<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/session\">会话</a>进行过程中切换。",
    "In practice, you change mode as your trust changes over the course of a task. The same task can pass through several modes: plan mode while the approach is still being shaped, the prompting default for the first delicate edits, accept-edits once the agent has shown it understands the change, bypass for an AFK run inside a sandbox. Changing mode costs you nothing: the conversation continues exactly where it was, with new permissions and new instructions. If you find yourself approving every prompt without reading it, the mode is set tighter than your actual trust; if you keep rejecting edits, it's set looser.": "实际使用中，应随着任务推进和信任程度变化切换模式。同一任务可以经历多个阶段：方案尚在打磨时使用规划模式；第一次进行谨慎编辑时使用会主动询问的默认模式；智能体已经证明理解改动后切换到自动接受编辑；在<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/sandbox\">沙箱</a>中进行 <a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/afk\">AFK</a> 运行时再切换到绕过权限。切换模式本身没有额外成本：对话会从原位置继续，只是权限和指令发生变化。如果你发现自己根本不看内容就批准每次询问，说明模式比实际信任程度更严格；如果你不断拒绝编辑，则说明模式过于宽松。",
    "The bundling is what distinguishes a mode from a bare permission setting. A permission mode is only a gate: it decides which tool calls go through. A gate alone produces an agent that wants to edit but can't — it proposes the write, gets blocked, and tries another way. The injected instructions remove the want: plan mode doesn't just block edits, it tells the agent it's in a planning phase, so it reads, asks, and proposes instead of straining against the gate. Gate and steer point the same direction.": "这种组合正是“模式”与单纯权限设置的区别。权限模式只是一道门：决定哪些<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/tool-call\">工具调用</a>可以通过。只有门控时，智能体仍想编辑，只是无法执行——它提出写入、遭到阻止，然后尝试绕路。注入的行为指令会从源头改变这种意图：规划模式不只是阻止编辑，还明确告诉智能体当前处于规划阶段，因此它会转向阅读、提问和提出方案，而不是不断冲撞权限门。门控与行为引导指向同一方向。",
    "Usage:": "<em>用法：</em>",
    "Vendor terms: Claude Code calls these \"permission modes,\" Codex calls them \"approval modes\" — both predate behavioral bundling.": "不同产品的叫法有所不同：Claude Code 称之为“permission modes（权限模式）”，Codex 称之为“approval modes（批准模式）”。这些名称都早于权限与行为指令开始组合的时期。"
  },
